From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:07:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: cpufreq: apple,cluster-cpufreq: Add
 apple,fast-die-effort

PMP publishes, per CPU cluster, how hard the host should limit the
cluster to hold the die at its temperature target. Name the PMP report
and the cluster's lane in it.

Based on Ryan Murray's binding in Aurora Silicon's tree (dd6da23a31d7).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 .../bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml        | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
index 32105bcc164f..211964efcc49 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
@@ -47,6 +47,16 @@ properties:
   '#performance-domain-cells':
     const: 0
 
+  apple,fast-die-effort:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    description: |
+      PMP report publishing the fast die-temperature effort, and this
+      cluster's lane in it. The effort limits the cluster's maximum frequency.
+    items:
+      - items:
+          - description: PMP report
+          - description: Cluster lane (0 for E, 1 for P on T8132)
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
